      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "642dbb0ae24b310a4a10c96d",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Not just for the camera IMHO, would make a lot of sense for vrc-rendering in general:\n\nThere's such a ton of worlds around forcing the creators OMGWTFBBQ postprocessing eyecandy & visual-fx onto you... dragging your fps down in the process... toggles? nope! deal with it! \n\nOk, I see \"but that might totally break the worlds look\" as argument against it and raise you one \"then why not lock these advanced options behind a warning - just like the unlimited mirror already does?\"\n\n:|\n\nAlso: pleeease(!), could we have an option to disable/toggle the cameras ingame viewfinder in streamcam-mode, if we chose so?\n\nAt least for me the complete camera-UI is constantly in the way when dancing, no matter where I \"drop & lock\" it (floor, sky, behind me etc), ontop of that rendering the viewfinder once it gets into your POV causes a hefty frametime-spike/drop of fps. :|\n\nMy preferred process when I want to stream would be:\n\n- enable streamcam\n\n- edit cam-options & position lense (maybe set a couple/pins)\n\n- disable ingame rendering of the camera UI/viewfinder & forget it ever was there\n\n- dance my ass off! \n\n\\m/\n\nAlso v2.0: an option to have the 5s-timer autoreapeat would make sense aswell, so you can put that UI away and focus on whatever you're doing instead of grabbing the UI and hitting the timer-button again every couple of seconds\n\nPrettyplease? <3 <3 <3",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
