        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For the love of god and all that is holy... THIS! 1000% this.  \n\nI legit had to put a color test card on my avatar to be able to overcome the awful color grading of some worlds. Some worlds I wouldn't even bother recording as it would not be possible to color correct. A lot of world creators really lean hard on PP and not in a good way.  \n\nI'm still stunned to my core that green screen function is effected by world pp.  That isn't how keying works.  I worked in SFX and seen my share of bad green screen lighting IRL but I think some of the places I tried to record in some worlds the PP takes the cake for worst key in the footage. \n\nIt would be nice to be able to override it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
